# Pentatonic Box 1 Lick (repertoire plan: st-pent-box-1). An original 8-bar study in A minor
# pentatonic box 1, frets 5 to 8, over a one-chord Am7 groove. Four 2-bar phrases in call and
# response: phrases 1 and 3 ask (they stop on G and on E, chord tones that leave the door open),
# phrases 2 and 4 answer (they come home to A). All 12 notes of the box are used, and nothing else.
# One finger per fret, as the Scales screen shows the box: finger 1 on fret 5, finger 3 on fret 7
# (strings 5, 4, 3), finger 4 on fret 8 (strings 6, 2, 1). The hand never moves.
# The hammer-on is in bar 6: string 3 fret 5 (C) to string 3 fret 7 (D).
title: Pentatonic Box 1 Lick
composer: Sixstring Academy
